(AFTER THE STOCK MARKET CRASH OF NOVEMBER, 1929) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(By way of comment on the great speculative epidemic that spread over) Tj T*
(the country and indeed throughout the world the past five or six years,) Tj T*
(it may be observed that stock speculation, once considered a hazardous) Tj T*
(business, came to be generally regarded as a safe, dignified and) Tj T*
(profitable occupation. Of a certainty it became general, if nothing) Tj T*
(else. From a once precarious game of chance, to be indulged in only by) Tj T*
(daredevils and millionaires, it became so simple and well safeguarded) Tj T*
(that anyone with a little capital could in a short time double it and) Tj T*
(quadruple it. It was contended that inasmuch as we had successfully) Tj T*
(passed the twenty-year cycle in which, according to precedent, stock) Tj T*
(market panics are wont to occur, such disturbances had been relegated) Tj T*
(to history, and the Federal Reserve System obviated any possibility of) Tj T*
(their recurrence. This belief pervaded all classes from millionaires) Tj T*
(to house servants, and eventually the entire community became) Tj T*
(inoculated with the speculative germ. It got to be the principal topic) Tj T*
(of conversation in the clubs, cafes, hotel lobbies, on the street, and) Tj T*
(any place where two or more people were congregated. The many thousands) Tj T*
(of brokerage offices throughout the country were jammed to the doors) Tj T*
(by eager onlookers and participants who devoted themselves exclusively) Tj T*
(to the market from the opening to the close. Office boys, elevator) Tj T*
(men, manicures, hotel waiters, hairdressers, cab drivers, and even) Tj T*
(rural farmers initiated themselves into the game and discussed mergers,) Tj T*
(split-ups, stock dividends, and all such subjects in high finance with) Tj T*
(more profuseness and profundity than was ever displayed at a bankers?) Tj T*
(convention.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Indeed for years it looked as if stocks could only go one way--up.) Tj T*
(Therefore the whole speculative fraternity arrayed itself on the) Tj T*
(up-side; and it actually happened that vast numbers of traders who) Tj T*
