(had formerly bought stocks to sell at only a point or two profit, now) Tj T*
(accumulated them to keep indefinitely. The trading element, emboldened) Tj T*
(by one success after another, concluded that we were in a new) Tj T*
(era--that the stock market millennium had become a reality. In travel) Tj T*
(we advanced from the stage coach to the automobile and the aeroplane;) Tj T*
(from the slow sailing craft to the ocean greyhound. The radio and the) Tj T*
(telephone had linked the whole universe together in conversation, and) Tj T*
(in the art of creating wealth the old-fashioned slow-moving process of) Tj T*
(conservatism had become as obsolete as the stage coach. These facts) Tj T*
(were all too obvious to be disputed. And to prove there was simply) Tj T*
(no limit to modern inventions the stock market, backed by the new) Tj T*
(investment trust scheme, supplied a new financial vehicle without) Tj T*
(any reverse gears. It was fast and easy riding, the sensation was) Tj T*
(thrilling, and it required neither skill nor experience to operate.) Tj T*
(In 1924-6 during the try-out period of this marvellous get-rich-quick) Tj T*
(machine there were many skeptics who doubted its safety and efficiency;) Tj T*
(but confidence gradually increased and one after another became) Tj T*
(convinced, until eventually the whole populace clambered aboard.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Business was good, the country was rich and prosperous, and it was) Tj T*
(argued that a financial structure built upon such confidence and) Tj T*
(prosperity could not be shaken by anything short of a universal) Tj T*
(earthquake. Basic values had become so stabilized in the minds of the) Tj T*
(people that there was no more reason to expect them to crumble than) Tj T*
(there was to expect the Washington Monument to topple over. Even the) Tj T*
(gray-haired wizards of Wall Street who had preached caution for two) Tj T*
(or three years, finally fell into line with the new order of things,) Tj T*
(and not only did they plunge into the market long after it had passed) Tj T*
(the point of safety, but they organized more investment trusts running) Tj T*
(into billions of dollars, and advertised far and wide for the public) Tj T*
(to buy their stock and join them in amassing fortunes. They would) Tj T*
(manage everything, and all the people had to do was to furnish the) Tj T*
(money. These cold-blooded Wall Street magnates, suddenly converted) Tj T*
(to the theory of universal brotherhood, undertook to espouse the) Tj T*
(cause in which everybody works for one another. Verily the Biblical) Tj T*
(prophecy was more than fulfilled; for it came to pass that not only) Tj T*
(could the lamb lie down in safety with the lion,--he could feed with) Tj T*
(him at the Wall Street manger. The public was thus taken into these) Tj T*
(co-operative partnerships and enabled to enjoy all the advantages to) Tj T*
(be derived from the superior genius and directorship of the giants) Tj T*
(of wealth and commerce. The small investors and speculators, highly) Tj T*
(flattered by the opportunity of being admitted into such society, threw) Tj T*
(their savings into the melting pot with more confidence than as if) Tj T*
(they were putting them into a savings bank. Many of the trusts were) Tj T*
(legitimate; others were disguised gambling pools operating on other) Tj T*
(people?s money, along the lines proposed by the late ?Tom? Lawson in) Tj T*
(the memorable advertising campaign he conducted in Bay State Gas.) Tj T*
(In most cases these gambling ventures were sponsored by names that) Tj T*
(inspired confidence; and those who bought participation certificates) Tj T*
(would undoubtedly have won if the stock market had never stopped going) Tj T*
(up. It was generally supposed that such men could not go financially) Tj T*
(wrong--and they didn?t; it was the public that went wrong in buying) Tj T*
