() Tj T*
(Many of these so-called investment trusts accumulated thousands upon) Tj T*
(thousands of highly speculative common shares that paid less than 2%) Tj T*
(income on their market value. Indeed one day in September, 1929, a) Tj T*
(statistician figured that the twelve most active stocks on the New) Tj T*
(York Stock Exchange averaged a return of only one and three-fifths) Tj T*
(per cent. on their selling price, and with no immediate prospect of) Tj T*
(increased dividends. With dozens of investment companies hoarding) Tj T*
(securities, all one had to do was buy the active stocks, hold them for) Tj T*
(a big rise, then unload them onto some new investment trust. The pot) Tj T*
(was kept boiling by all sorts of rumors of stock dividends, split-ups,) Tj T*
(consolidations and such-like enticements; and when things quieted) Tj T*
(down a bit, someone would bring out the old reliable rumor that while) Tj T*
(the public was taking a breathing spell the big bankers were quietly) Tj T*
(accumulating large lines. It worked like magic on the inflamed public) Tj T*
(mind--it always does. If the bankers are buying, why shouldn?t the) Tj T*
(public buy? Another popular device was to broadcast reports accredited) Tj T*
(to Messrs. Coolidge & Mellon, to the effect that after scanning the) Tj T*
(speculative horizon they could discover no reason why the market should) Tj T*
(not keep on going up. With such a bulwark of confidence there was but) Tj T*
(little reason to be afraid. It did not matter whether stocks paid small) Tj T*
(dividends, or no dividends. It did not matter if money loaned at ten,) Tj T*
(twelve, or fifteen per cent. The rise in values would take care of) Tj T*
(all that, with ample to spare. Frequently one day?s advance in price) Tj T*
(would cover a whole year?s interest or more. Nor did it matter that) Tj T*
(brokers? commissions had nearly doubled, and that this gigantic ?kitty?) Tj T*
(was taking millions of dollars in toll every day. It works on the same) Tj T*
(principle as poker: if seven players sit into a game with a ?kitty,?) Tj T*
(it?s only a question of time when at least six of them will go broke.) Tj T*
(I heard one trader proudly declare that in three years he had paid his) Tj T*
(broker upward of half a million dollars in commissions, and nearly) Tj T*
(twice that amount in interest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Now and again the brokers? letters and the comments of financial) Tj T*
(editors contained notes of warning, but the public having got the bit) Tj T*
(firmly in its teeth was like a runaway team: it could neither see) Tj T*
(nor hear anything that stood in the way of progress. Facts were more) Tj T*
(conclusive than theories; and since those arrayed on the constructive) Tj T*
(side had all the advantage in their favor for an almost uninterrupted) Tj T*
(period of several years, they indulged themselves in a delirium of) Tj T*
(dreams from which there appeared to be no awakening. It was as useless) Tj T*
