(stocks were very scarce; that they had nearly all gone into ?strong) Tj T*
(hands;? that they were locked up in strong boxes, and nothing could) Tj T*
(shake them out. To test the truth of this story, I made inquiries among) Tj T*
(several brokers and traders of my acquaintance, with this result:) Tj T*
(I found that almost without exception, traders were carrying more) Tj T*
(securities on margin than they had ever owned before, and that a vast) Tj T*
(number of them were pyramiding on their profits. I personally knew one) Tj T*
(man who prior to Coolidge?s election had never carried more than two or) Tj T*
(three hundred shares, but thereafter he began buying, and continued to) Tj T*
