(Among the curious aftermaths of the 1929 crash, was a profusion of) Tj T*
(printed articles by well known ?financial experts,? each one searching) Tj T*
(vainly to find some explanation of what caused the great cataclysm.) Tj T*
(Some laid it onto President Hoover, some fixed the responsibility on) Tj T*
(the Federal Reserve Board, while others attributed it to one cause and) Tj T*
(another; but no one seems to have guessed that it was the distorted) Tj T*
(psychology of the traders themselves that brought about their own ruin.) Tj T*
(Since nobody likes to be told that he?s wrong, perhaps those who lost) Tj T*
(their money found some consolation in reading authoritative opinions) Tj T*
(that the blame was chargeable to some one other than themselves.) Tj T*
(One eminent economist has lately written many pages of more or less) Tj T*
(convincing argument to prove that the liquidation started in London,) Tj T*
(Paris and Berlin--as if it made any real difference where or how it) Tj T*
(started. The survivors of a storm-swept area \(also the speculators\) are) Tj T*
(more concerned with what happened than they are with how the storm) Tj T*
(began or where it came from.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is one great mystery worthy of comment; and that is, how such a) Tj T*
(tremendous scaling down in values could have been accomplished in so) Tj T*
(short a time without bankrupting a single one of the major banks or) Tj T*
(brokerage firms. The answer must be that the public stood the loss--as) Tj T*
(it usually does. And why not? They had every chance in the world to get) Tj T*
(out with fabulous profits. For more than a year they had the advice,) Tj T*
(warning and threats of the Federal Reserve Board displayed on the pages) Tj T*
(of all the newspapers, and dinned into their ears. But whenever these) Tj T*
(warnings or any other danger signal appeared, the market manipulators) Tj T*
(showed their contempt by promptly pushing prices up a few more points.) Tj T*
(They defied and scoffed at every principle of common sense and business) Tj T*
(economics, and they got away with it so long and successfully that) Tj T*
(it seemed they were bound by no laws or limitations except those of) Tj T*
(their own devising. For years the market was under the dominion of a) Tj T*
(new generation of dare-devil cliques who manipulated it with an iron) Tj T*
(arm more daring and more dogmatic than the rule of any tyrant in) Tj T*
(history; and month after month the cool-headed non-participants read) Tj T*
(the financial pages with gaping amazement. If the weekly bank statement) Tj T*
(showed that brokers? loans had increased a hundred millions or more) Tj T*
(beyond expectations, it was the signal for a new outburst of bullish) Tj T*
(enthusiasm; if the interest rates were advanced or even doubled,) Tj T*
(millions of shares were immediately churned back and forth at advancing) Tj T*
(prices, in order to prove that the laws of gravity and economics had) Tj T*
(become subservient to the will of the speculative mob. It happened) Tj T*
(repeatedly that after some large corporation had issued an unexpectedly) Tj T*
(poor earnings statement, the stock of that company was immediately) Tj T*
(taken in hand and forced up several points, on the argument that the) Tj T*
(?bad news is all out,? and had already been fully discounted. And on) Tj T*
(the theory that a storm-tossed ship is more apt to sink if standing) Tj T*
(still than if running under full steam, the market was pushed ahead at) Tj T*
