() Tj T*
(The theory advanced by some of the economists that the trading public) Tj T*
(merely lost their paper profits, and practically nothing else was) Tj T*
(either gained or lost in the tremendous rise and fall of stocks,) Tj T*
(is a little misleading. One authority says: ?For the shrinkage of) Tj T*
(thirty-five or forty billions of dollars in stock exchange securities) Tj T*
(nobody is any poorer but on account of things possessed and consumed) Tj T*
(too soon.? Assuming that the market started at a given point in 1924) Tj T*
(and reacted to that point in 1929, it would mean a loss of many) Tj T*
(hundreds of millions in commissions and interest. It is estimated that) Tj T*
(in 1929 alone the commissions for transactions on the two ?Big Boards?) Tj T*
(amounted to well upward of five hundred million dollars. Most of the) Tj T*
(margin traders lost all of their original investment, and many of them) Tj T*
(all they could borrow on their notes, their life insurance policies,) Tj T*
(and even their homes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All this by way of retrospect. The vital question that confronts us) Tj T*
(is: will traders and investors profit by the experience? Apparently) Tj T*
(not. The survivors of the late catastrophe promptly formed a ?wrecking) Tj T*
(crew,? and are at the present moment busily engaged in rebuilding the) Tj T*
(market structure on pretty much the same lines as before. The rumor) Tj T*
(band has been reorganized and is piping its old-time music into the) Tj T*
(ears of all listeners. The tipsters are also lined up, and with the) Tj T*
(cheery cry that the storm is all over they are wheedling and coaxing) Tj T*
(the public to come out of the storm cellars and get aboard the) Tj T*
(reconstruction train. They harp persistently on the fact that stocks) Tj T*
(are cheap,--not because of their dividend return, but because they) Tj T*
(are selling much below the boom prices. Their calculations are drawn) Tj T*
(mostly from figures at the big end of the measuring tape. Improved) Tj T*
(business--which exists more in the imagination than in fact--is) Tj T*
(employed as a smoke screen to hide the fact that the great majority of) Tj T*
(the active stocks are still selling far above a reasonable investment) Tj T*
(basis. At their present prices ten of the best known representative) Tj T*
(common stocks,--U. S. Steel, General Electric, Westinghouse Electric,) Tj T*
(Atchison, American Tobacco, Radio, Consolidated Gas, American & Foreign) Tj T*
(Power, Columbia Gas and Johns-Manville, pay an average return of two) Tj T*
(and nine-tenths per cent. In other words, at going prices if you bought) Tj T*
(one share each of these ten stocks the total cost would be $1425 on) Tj T*
(which you would receive an annual dividend of $41.60, or less than the) Tj T*
(return on U. S. Government bonds. It is therefore clear that a bull) Tj T*
(market constructed on this basis must be a highly speculative affair.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In February, 1930, the financial editor of the New York Herald Tribune) Tj T*
(printed the following comment:--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?The upward pace of the stock market leads one to believe that the) Tj T*
